WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.467
Planning a sunset, or a night under the stars?

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:07.020
LumiRaw's sky planner works it out for any spot on Earth.

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:10.093
Click the map, or type in the coordinates.

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:14.187
This is the Javalambre range in Spain, home to an observatory,

00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:16.829
and some of the darkest skies in Europe.

00:00:17.229 --> 00:00:20.565
You get the golden and blue hours, morning and evening,

00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:25.418
and the paths of the sun and moon over the horizon, at whatever time you choose,

00:00:25.418 --> 00:00:27.359
with the forecast's cloud cover.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.376
Best nights looks at the weeks ahead:

00:00:40.376 --> 00:00:44.800
how long the sky stays moonless each night, and how cloudy it's likely to be.

00:00:45.402 --> 00:00:48.495
Dark skies shows the light pollution around your spot,

00:00:48.495 --> 00:00:51.072
and can find the darkest places within reach.

00:00:56.399 --> 00:01:01.032
And sharp stars works out the longest exposure before the stars start to trail,

00:01:01.032 --> 00:01:04.609
for your camera and lens, with a preview of how they'll look.
